.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_BEGIN_MPQE 3 2026-09-28 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_begin_mpqe \- begin creating an MPQE-wrapped patch archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__patch_begin_mpqe(mpq_patch_s **patch, const char *base_archive, const char *output_patch, const uint8_t *auth_code, size_t auth_code_size);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a staged MPQE-wrapped patch artifact using an ordinary filesystem MPQ at \fIbase_archive\fP. The base remains unchanged. The caller supplies the authentication code used by the existing MPQE container writer; the code need only remain valid during this call. A matching code is required to read or apply the finished patch. Patch members retain the ordinary PTCH/COPY/BSD0 semantics. Finish publishes the encrypted artifact; abort discards it. Both operations consume the patch handle, even on error. On failure, a valid \fIpatch\fP output is set to NULL. This operation does not sign the patch or provide full Blizzard patch-metadata compatibility. Embedded and MPQE base archives are unsupported for patch creation.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
Invalid arguments, authentication-code errors, unsupported base formats, allocation failures, and I/O errors may propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__patch_begin (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_replace_data (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_remove (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_finish (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_abort (3)
